# Package Conventions

## Naming

Package names follow the pattern `@databricks/sdk-<dirname>`:

| Directory             | Package name                  |
| --------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| `packages/auth/`      | `@databricks/sdk-auth`        |
| `packages/databricks/` | `@databricks/sdk-databricks` |

## Required Files for a New Package

Every workspace package must contain these files:

```
packages/<name>/
├── src/
│   └── index.ts              # Package entry point
├── tests/
│   └── tsconfig.json         # REQUIRED — see below
├── package.json
├── tsconfig.json
└── vitest.config.browser.ts
```

### tests/tsconfig.json (critical)

Each package **must** have a `tests/tsconfig.json`. Without it, ESLint's
`@typescript-eslint/parser` with `project: true` cannot resolve test files
because the package-level `tsconfig.json` only includes `src/`.

```json
{
  "extends": "../../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": ".."
  },
  "include": [".", "../src"],
  "exclude": ["../dist", "../node_modules"]
}
```

### package.json

Copy from an existing package (e.g. `packages/auth/package.json`) and adjust
the `name`, `description`, and `exports` fields. Keep the same `devDependencies`
versions.

### tsconfig.json

```json
{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "outDir": "./dist",
    "rootDir": "./src"
  },
  "include": ["src"],
  "exclude": ["dist", "node_modules", "tests"]
}
```

## Exports

Use **subpath exports only**. Each submodule is imported via its own path.
Do not re-export children from parent `index.ts` files — this avoids a flat
namespace that grows unwieldy and risks name collisions.

```json
{
  "exports": {
    ".": { "types": "./dist/index.d.ts", "import": "./dist/index.js" },
    "./apierror": { "types": "./dist/apierror/index.d.ts", "import": "./dist/apierror/index.js" },
    "./apierror/codes": { "types": "./dist/apierror/codes/index.d.ts", "import": "./dist/apierror/codes/index.js" }
  }
}
```

## Verification Checklist

After creating a new package, run all four checks:

```bash
npm run build   --workspace=packages/<name>
npm run lint    --workspace=packages/<name>
npm run typecheck --workspace=packages/<name>
npm test        --workspace=packages/<name>
```
